cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this model, please cite it, and also credit the base model and the
  training dataset listed under `references`.
title: 'Azerbaijani TTS: an offline 9.36M-parameter VITS model'
abstract: >-
  A fully offline text-to-speech model for Azerbaijani. 9.36M parameters,
  24 kHz mono, single speaker, 2-4x faster than real time on a laptop CPU.
  Adapted from the English Inflect-Micro-v2 checkpoint over 200,000 steps on
  25.07 hours of Azerbaijani audio, and shipped with an Azerbaijani text
  normalisation and chunking layer.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Huseynli
    given-names: Ilqar
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/INSERT_GITHUB_USER/azerbaycan-tts'
keywords:
  - text-to-speech
  - speech-synthesis
  - azerbaijani
  - vits
  - offline
  - low-resource-languages

references:
  - type: software
    title: 'Inflect-Micro-v2'
    abstract: >-
      The English 9.36M-parameter VITS checkpoint this model was adapted from.
      409 of its 410 tensors were carried over bit-identically.
    authors:
      - family-names: Song
        given-names: Owen
    version: 2.0.0
    date-released: 2026-07-24
    url: 'https://huggingface.co/owensong/Inflect-Micro-v2'
    license: Apache-2.0

  - type: data
    title: 'azerbaijani-tts-dataset'
    abstract: >-
      The Azerbaijani speech corpus this model was trained on: 9,674 clips used
      out of 10,088, 25.07 hours, single speaker. The repository declares no
      licence file; the author confirmed in the Hugging Face community tab that
      the dataset may be used freely, with attribution requested.
    authors:
      - alias: ughurabbasov
    url: 'https://huggingface.co/datasets/ughurabbasov/azerbaijani-tts-dataset'
    notes: >-
      Used with the author's permission, granted in the dataset's Hugging Face
      community tab. Attribution is the condition of use.
